id: pm-ts-starter-sdk-contract-drift
title: Compile consumer examples against minimum and current SDK contracts
description: Add a typed public SDK compatibility matrix and CLI command for author-controlled consumer examples. Dependabot continues to own dependency bumps; starter pin checks continue to own installation acceptance.
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-24T10:33:04.255Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T10:43:46.760Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: A deliberately removed API fails its consumer fixture; packed npm and Bun runs compile against the emitted public contract; plain trackers work without git and remain unchanged.
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-24T10:33:06.485Z",codex-agent,"Overlap recheck: CLI scaffold author-time tsc and runtime-public-contract snapshots do not compare consumer examples across published SDK releases. Both starters test peer floors and installation; no sibling source implements this matrix. Dependabot retains all version bumps. Design: explicit exact-version installed SDK targets, real compiler processes, bounded path-free diagnostic rows, SDK-native command rendering and expected errors. Private per-call scratch only; no tracker writes, shared leases, checkpoints or caches."
  "2026-10-24T10:42:25.042Z",codex-agent,"Implemented typed compiler matrix, native TOON/JSON command, stable refusals, docs and example. Revert proof: changed only checkSdkContracts to report compiler failures as success (the former installation-only behavior); node --test --test-name-pattern=\"real SDK examples pass\" test/sdk-contracts.test.ts failed 1/1 (expected one failing current authoring fixture, got zero). Restored implementation. Targeted SDK+smoke run passed 101/101; targeted module measured 100% lines/branches/functions. Full npm/Bun release gates reserved for CI because the shared host is saturated."
  "2026-10-24T10:43:46.018Z",codex-agent,"Validation receipt: public origin/main f657fe38f18201c0eed07caa8613142fa0736984 copied to a non-git scratch tracker, made read-only, and read through the shipped complete-read consumer using both untouched npm SDKs 2026.10.17 and 2026.10.24 with git absent from PATH. Both certified 82 items (74 closed, 3 open, 2 in_progress, 2 canceled, 1 blocked). All 171 files / 1254538 bytes retained identical SHA-256 inventory 7468c3e9a1833d0e4e97232ed02335c94b41cf908f38d53d889dcabf530a81bf. Compiler matrix: 4 checks, 0 failures. Packed npm/Bun consumers each compiled 6 endpoint/example pairs, including emitted index declarations; installed CLI returned JSON and TOON without git. Six execution boundaries each injected a peer SDK tracker update and successful peer matrix; original record and peer success survived. pm test --run --progress passed 7/7, with 100% module lines/branches/functions; result tracking is disabled by existing project policy, so this comment retains the receipt. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstrings and zero-duplication checks passed."
files[3]{path,scope}:
  index.ts,project
  sdk-contracts.ts,project
  test/sdk-contracts.test.ts,project
tests[1]{command,scope,provenance{author,created_at,source_kind,source_ref}}:
